      "media_slot_id": "ML-IM.cover.steen",
      "heading": "Master Lecture · Image morphology",
      "sentence": "Describe dot, line, plane, shape, form, colour, composition, and perspective before semantics.",
      "prompt": "Foundational visual vocabulary for I1–I5 and the analysis master class",
      "quote": "Describe first. Interpret later.",
      "quote_origin": "tao_invented",
      "semantic_tags": { "themes": ["master-lecture", "analysis", "fashion-image"] }
    },
    {
      "slide_role": "analysis_opener",
      "background_kind": "profield",
      "media_slot_id": "ML-IM.opener.takahashi",
      "heading": "Morphology · formal inventory",
      "sentence": "Name what is visible before you infer what it means."
    },
    {
      "slide_role": "analysis_model",
      "background_kind": "profield",
      "media_slot_id": "ML-IM.sequence.dylan-dress",
      "heading": "Morphology sequence",
      "sentence": "Dot → line → plane → shape → form → colour → composition → space/perspective.",
      "prompt": "Stop after formal evidence. Critical interpretation belongs to the sibling analysis master class."
    },
    {
      "slide_role": "masterclass",
      "background_kind": "profield",
      "media_slot_id": "ML-FIA.morphology.dot",
      "heading": "1 · Dot — locate attention",
      "sentence": "Find the smallest event that arrests the eye before naming its meaning.",
      "prompt": "Describe position, scale, repetition, and contrast."
    },
    {
      "slide_role": "masterclass",
      "background_kind": "profield",
      "media_slot_id": "ML-FIA.morphology.line",
      "heading": "2 · Line — follow movement",
      "sentence": "Trace contour, direction, gesture, and force: the line makes looking move.",
      "prompt": "Ask what the line joins, divides, or makes dynamic."
    },
    {
      "slide_role": "masterclass",
      "background_kind": "profield",
      "media_slot_id": "ML-FIA.morphology.plane",
      "heading": "3 · Plane and shape — organise fields",
      "sentence": "Separate figure/ground, layers, and bounded silhouettes before interpreting them.",
      "quote": "Photographic images play a key role in defining global fashion culture and in charting its discursive space.",
      "quote_origin": "page_verified",
      "citation": {
        "label": "(Shinkle 2008, 14)",
        "href": "/lessons/en/master-lectures/fashion-image-analysis/#references"
      }
    },
    {
      "slide_role": "masterclass",
      "background_kind": "profield",
      "media_slot_id": "ML-FIA.morphology.form",
      "heading": "4 · Form — test volume",
      "sentence": "Read mass, edge, light, and fold: what appears flat, folded, or volumetric?",
      "quote": "there is no single and easily described genre of 'fashion photography'. Equally, there is no single methodology which is best suited to its analysis",
      "quote_origin": "page_verified",
      "citation": {
        "label": "(Shinkle 2008, 17)",
        "href": "/lessons/en/master-lectures/fashion-image-analysis/#references"
      }
    },
    {
      "slide_role": "masterclass",
      "background_kind": "profield",
      "media_slot_id": "ML-FIA.morphology.colour",
      "heading": "5 · Colour — compare relations",
      "sentence": "Name hue, value, saturation, temperature, and contrast before assigning emotion.",
      "quote": "Colour is the keyboard. The eye is the hammer, while the soul is a piano of many strings.",
      "quote_origin": "page_verified",
      "citation": {
        "label": "(Kandinsky 1946, 44)",
        "href": "/lessons/en/master-lectures/image-morphology/#ref-kandinsky-1946"
      },
      "prompt": "Compare hue, value, saturation, temperature, and contrast without assigning emotion."
    },
    {
